cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use these certificates, scripts, or results, please cite this
  repository as below, using the version DOI of the part you rely on:
  Part A (Alpöge Keller map) v0.1.x doi:10.5281/zenodo.21799112; Part B
  (quantum code distances) v0.2.0 doi:10.5281/zenodo.21799780; Part C
  (tournament packing) v0.3.0 doi:10.5281/zenodo.21816010; Part D
  ([[14,3,5]] automorphism exclusion) v0.4.0 doi:10.5281/zenodo.21816018.
  The concept DOI below resolves to the latest version. For Part A,
  credit for the underlying counterexample map belongs to Levent Alpöge
  (announcement of 2026-07-19; problem posed by Akhil Mathew); the
  Dixmier corollary AND the symplectic cotangent lift are both due to
  W. G. P. Mayner (2026-07-20/21); the master equation, the base-point
  (anchor) identity, the S_3 monodromy and the exact image theorem are
  anticipated by T. Shaska (arXiv:2607.20210), the anonymous note at
  ulam.ai/research/jacobian.pdf, MathOverflow 513387, and Mayner. What
  this repository claims as new in Part A is the in-class
  degree-minimality theorem, the moment-map identity, and the no-go
  lemma. See PROVENANCE.md §2 and §2b. Part A v0.1.2 (2026-08-06) is an
  erratum release: it corrects the Theorem D fiber count over
  {Delta_2 = 0} to three distinct points (the set-theoretic fiber sizes
  are {3, 1, 0}, not {3, 2, 1}); {Delta_2 = 0} is an apparent branch
  locus. No other claim depended on it. v0.1.2 supersedes v0.1.0 and
  v0.1.1 on this point only; see paper/ERRATUM-v0.1.2.md and the scripts
  in scripts/erratum-check/. For Parts B–D, credit statements are in the
  README and in each note.
type: software
title: >-
  Certify: replayable certificates for machine-checked mathematics
  (degree minimality of the Alpöge Keller map; certified quantum code
  distances; the tournament packing numbers nu_3(9), nu_3(10); a
  [[14,3,5]] automorphism exclusion)
authors:
