references:
  - type: generic
    title: A counterexample to the Jacobian conjecture in dimension three
    authors:
      - family-names: Alpöge
        given-names: Levent
    date-published: "2026-07-19"
    notes: Public announcement; see the Secret Blogging Seminar and Tao posts.
  - type: generic
    title: >-
      The Dixmier conjecture fails for A_n, n >= 3 (dixmier-note.tex) and
      Structural analysis of the Jacobian conjecture counterexample in C^3
      (REPORT.md)
    authors:
      - family-names: Mayner
        given-names: W. G. P.
    date-published: "2026-07-21"
    url: "https://github.com/wmayner/dixmier-counterexample"
    notes: >-
      Two commits, 2026-07-21 05:36 and 06:41 UTC. The Dixmier statement was
      first made in a Secret Blogging Seminar comment of 2026-07-20, 22:08.
      REPORT.md section 8 contains the symplectic cotangent lift with
      Phi*omega = omega exactly, det DPhi = 1, and non-injectivity, listed in
      its priority section 12 as item 3. Not on arXiv; no DOI.
  - type: article
    title: Graded Keller maps and the Jacobian Conjecture
    authors:
      - family-names: Shaska
        given-names: T.
    date-published: "2026-07-22"
    url: "https://arxiv.org/abs/2607.20210"
    notes: >-
      v1 2026-07-22, v2 2026-07-25. v2 Thm 8.3 is the master equation, v2
      Lem 8.5 the base-point identity, v1 Thm 6.1 = v2 Thm 7.1 the
      order-two vanishing on the contracted locus, v1 Thm 4.4(2) the S_3
      monodromy, v1 Prop 5.1 the fiber counts and missed curve.
  - type: generic
    title: A counterexample to the Jacobian conjecture
    authors:
      - name: "Anonymous"
    date-published: "2026-07-20"
    url: "https://ulam.ai/research/jacobian.pdf"
    notes: >-
      Thm 4.2 gives the fiber counts 3/1/0 and the image complement
      explicitly; Thm 5.1 and Cor 5.3 give families of every generic degree
      at least 3. PDF timestamp 2026-07-20 05:54 EDT.
